# Electronic Resources in the Humanities.

**Authors:** Benaud, Claire-Lise, Bordeianu, Sever

## Abstract
Examines the role of electronic sources in the humanities. Topics include characteristics of humanities, electronic resources in libraries, two bibliographic utilities, library online catalogs, commercial online databases, CD-ROMs, resources on the Internet, discussion lists, electronic journals, full-text databases, research centers, informal communication, and implications for libraries. (57 references) (AEF)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ501772

